From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim 'mithro' Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 20:19:43 +0930
Subject: [PATCH 22/32] main: flash-info JSON version 2

The contract says version is increased whenever a field changes meaning,
and 9b682b6 changed "sfdp": null from "no SFDP, or the SFDP read failed"
to "the part has no SFDP" only. A consumer can now tell a version 2
null (positive evidence the part does not implement RSFDP) from a
version 1 one. Version 2 documents also carry extended_id. The doc lists
what each version means.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F2L6L5SJYvbBUUt4DinjGC
---
 doc/guide/advanced.rst | 8 +++++++-
 src/main.cpp           | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/guide/advanced.rst b/doc/guide/advanced.rst
index 884871c..5d26a98 100644
--- a/doc/guide/advanced.rst
+++ b/doc/guide/advanced.rst
@@ -117,7 +117,7 @@ file and a zero exit status mean the content was read:
 
 .. code-block:: json
 
-    {"format": "openFPGALoader-flash-info", "version": 1, "flashes": [
+    {"format": "openFPGALoader-flash-info", "version": 2, "flashes": [
       {"jedec_id": "0x010219", "manufacturer_id": "0x01", "memory_type": "0x02",
        "capacity": "0x19", "manufacturer": "Spansion",
        "manufacturer_jep106": "Spansion / Cypress / Infineon",
@@ -178,6 +178,12 @@ fields may be added without a new ``version``: ignore unknown fields. The
 openFPGALoader version string does not tell whether ``--flash-info`` is
 available: check for ``--flash-info-json`` in ``--help`` instead.
 
+Versions:
+
+* ``1``: first version. ``sfdp`` could be ``null`` after a failed SFDP read.
+* ``2``: ``sfdp`` is ``null`` only when the part has no SFDP (a failed read
+  is an error), and ``extended_id`` is added.
+
 .. NOTE::
   On FPGAs where the flash is only reachable through the FPGA (ie Xilinx,
   through a *spiOverJtag* bridge), every ``--flash-info`` read, including the
diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index a13a78b..a687a72 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -160,7 +160,7 @@ static bool write_flash_info_json(const std::string &path)
 		return false;
 	}
 	std::string j = "{\"format\": \"openFPGALoader-flash-info\", "
-		"\"version\": 1, \"flashes\": [";
+		"\"version\": 2, \"flashes\": [";
 	for (size_t i = 0; i < recs.size(); i++)
 		j += (i ? ", " : "") + recs[i];
 	j += "]}\n";
